vents{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2021-10-07T21:36:43Z","label":{"name":"bug","color":"d73a4a"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/938175563","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7160#issuecomment-938175563","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7160","id":938175563,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB84362xL","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-10-07T21:40:41Z","updated_at":"2021-10-07T21:43:42Z","body":"hi as youll note SQLAlchemy is not able to receive information from SQL Server regarding this foreign key constraint.   Generating your tables as follows using alembic:\r\n\r\n```sql\r\nCREATE TABLE [BaseTable] (\r\n\tid BIGINT NOT NULL IDENTITY, \r\n\tname NVARCHAR(50) NOT NULL, \r\n\tPRIMARY KEY (id)\r\n)\r\n\r\n\r\nINFO  [sqlalchemy.engine.Engine] [no key 0.00021s] ()\r\nINFO  [sqlalchemy.engine.Engine] CREATE UNIQUE INDEX [UK_BaseTable_name] ON [BaseTable] (name)\r\nINFO  [sqlalchemy.engine.Engine] [no key 0.00020s] ()\r\nINFO  [sqlalchemy.engine.Engine] \r\nCREATE TABLE [SideTable] (\r\n\tid BIGINT NOT NULL IDENTITY, \r\n\tmother_id BIGINT NULL, \r\n\tmother_name NVARCHAR(50) NOT NULL, \r\n\tPRIMARY KEY (id), \r\n\tFOREIGN KEY(mother_id) REFERENCES [BaseTable] (id), \r\n\tFOREIGN KEY(mother_name) REFERENCES [BaseTable] (name)\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nwe see what's special about the second FK is that it targets a column that's not in the primary key of the table, it just has a unique index (which in my experience also constrains it uniquely but perhaps SQL Server has some strange behavior here?) on it.  im not sure that we have a standard test suite that specifically targets that style of FK, but at least in this case it does not seem to work on SQL Server.  The query we issue and the result returned by SQL server can be seen in the session below:\r\n\r\n```py\r\nIn [1]: from sqlalchemy import create_engine\r\n\r\nIn [2]: e = create_engine(\"mssql+pyodbc://scott:tiger^5HHH@mssql2017:1433/test?driver=ODBC+Driver+13+for+SQL+Server\", echo='debug')\r\n\r\nIn [3]: from sqlalchemy import inspect\r\n\r\nIn [4]: i = inspect(e)\r\n2021-10-07 17:34:18,463 INFO sqlalchemy.engine.Engine SELECT CAST(SERVERPROPERTY('ProductVersion') AS VARCHAR)\r\n2021-10-07 17:34:18,463 INFO sqlalchemy.engine.Engine [raw sql] ()\r\n2021-10-07 17:34:18,465 DEBUG sqlalchemy.engine.Engine Col ('',)\r\n2021-10-07 17:34:18,465 DEBUG sqlalchemy.engine.Engine Row ('14.0.3356.20',)\r\n2021-10-07 17:34:18,466 INFO sqlalchemy.engine.Engine SELECT schema_name()\r\n2021-10-07 17:34:18,466 INFO sqlalchemy.engine.Engine [generated in 0.00019s] ()\r\n2021-10-07 17:34:18,468 DEBUG sqlalchemy.engine.Engine Col ('',)\r\n2021-10-07 17:34:18,468 DEBUG sqlalchemy.engine.Engine Row ('scott',)\r\n2021-10-07 17:34:18,470 INFO sqlalchemy.engine.Engine SELECT CAST('test max support' AS NVARCHAR(max))\r\n2021-10-07 17:34:18,470 INFO sqlalchemy.engine.Engine [generated in 0.00022s] ()\r\n2021-10-07 17:34:18,472 DEBUG sqlalchemy.engine.Engine Col ('',)\r\n2021-10-07 17:34:18,472 DEBUG sqlalchemy.engine.Engine Row ('test max support',)\r\n\r\nIn [5]: i.get_foreign_keys(\"SideTable\")\r\n2021-10-07 17:34:37,115 INFO sqlalchemy.engine.Engine SELECT [C].[COLUMN_NAME], [R].[TABLE_SCHEMA], [R].[TABLE_NAME], [R].[COLUMN_NAME] AS [COLUMN_NAME_1], [INFORMATION_SCHEMA].[REFERENTIAL_CONSTRAINTS].[CONSTRAINT_NAME], [INFORMATION_SCHEMA].[REFERENTIAL_CONSTRAINTS].[MATCH_OPTION], [INFORMATION_SCHEMA].[REFERENTIAL_CONSTRAINTS].[UPDATE_RULE], [INFORMATION_SCHEMA].[REFERENTIAL_CONSTRAINTS].[DELETE_RULE] \r\nFROM [INFORMATION_SCHEMA].[KEY_COLUMN_USAGE] AS [C], [INFORMATION_SCHEMA].[KEY_COLUMN_USAGE] AS [R], [INFORMATION_SCHEMA].[REFERENTIAL_CONSTRAINTS] \r\nWHERE [C].[TABLE_NAME] = CAST(? AS NVARCHAR(max)) AND [C].[TABLE_SCHEMA] = CAST(? AS NVARCHAR(max)) AND [INFORMATION_SCHEMA].[REFERENTIAL_CONSTRAINTS].[CONSTRAINT_SCHEMA] = [C].[TABLE_SCHEMA] AND [C].[CONSTRAINT_NAME] = [INFORMATION_SCHEMA].[REFERENTIAL_CONSTRAINTS].[CONSTRAINT_NAME] AND [R].[CONSTRAINT_NAME] = [INFORMATION_SCHEMA].[REFERENTIAL_CONSTRAINTS].[UNIQUE_CONSTRAINT_NAME] AND [R].[CONSTRAINT_SCHEMA] = [INFORMATION_SCHEMA].[REFERENTIAL_CONSTRAINTS].[UNIQUE_CONSTRAINT_SCHEMA] AND [C].[ORDINAL_POSITION] = [R].[ORDINAL_POSITION] ORDER BY [INFORMATION_SCHEMA].[REFERENTIAL_CONSTRAINTS].[CONSTRAINT_NAME], [R].[ORDINAL_POSITION]\r\n2021-10-07 17:34:37,115 INFO sqlalchemy.engine.Engine [generated in 0.00070s] ('SideTable', 'scott')\r\n2021-10-07 17:34:37,259 DEBUG sqlalchemy.engine.Engine Col ('COLUMN_NAME', 'TABLE_SCHEMA', 'TABLE_NAME', 'COLUMN_NAME_1', 'CONSTRAINT_NAME', 'MATCH_OPTION', 'UPDATE_RULE', 'DELETE_RULE')\r\n2021-10-07 17:34:37,261 DEBUG sqlalchemy.engine.Engine Row ('mother_id', 'scott', 'BaseTable', 'id', 'FK__SideTable__mothe__28D80438', 'SIMPLE', 'NO ACTION', 'NO ACTION')\r\nOut[5]: \r\n[{'name': 'FK__SideTable__mothe__28D80438',\r\n  'constrained_columns': ['mother_id'],\r\n  'referred_schema': None,\r\n  'referred_table': 'BaseTable',\r\n  'referred_columns': ['id']}]\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nabove we can see there's only one FK coming back, nothing about the second one.   We'd need to know how to query information schema to get info on that other one.  cc @gordthompson ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/938175563/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":5431208935,"node_id":"MEE_lADOCX5JB84801Z4zwAAAAFDuavn","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/events/5431208935","actor":{"login":"gordthompson","id":15894006,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1ODk0MDA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15894006?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gordthompson","html_url":"https://github.com/gordthompson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com